# Checklists

Purpose: release gates only. Detailed standards live in owner files in [`index.mdc`](./index.mdc).

## Release readiness

- [ ] Structure matches [`project_structure.mdc`](./project_structure.mdc)
- [ ] Layer boundaries per [`architecture.mdc`](./architecture.mdc)
- [ ] Dependencies per [`dependencies.mdc`](./dependencies.mdc)
- [ ] Theme/tokens per [`design-system.mdc`](./design-system.mdc)
- [ ] Components per [`components.mdc`](./components.mdc)
- [ ] Layouts/shell per [`layouts.mdc`](./layouts.mdc)
- [ ] Module workspaces per [`ui-workspace.mdc`](./ui-workspace.mdc) (new/changed queue screens)
- [ ] Localization: no hard-coded user-facing strings; no `_FeatureText` private copy classes
- [ ] Auth/permissions align with backend entitlements
- [ ] Entity refs: UI/API use `human_friendly_id` only ([`data_modeling.mdc`](./data_modeling.mdc))
- [ ] Subscription ∩ role permission intersection enforced ([`permissions.mdc`](./permissions.mdc), `.cursor/access/subscriptions.mdc`)
- [ ] Menus/routes/actions hidden for unauthorized users (strict RBAC+ABAC)
- [ ] API integration per [`.cursor/api-contract.mdc`](../../.cursor/api-contract.mdc)
- [ ] `flutter analyze` and `flutter test` pass ([`ci_cd_quality_gates.mdc`](./ci_cd_quality_gates.mdc))

## Per-feature gate

- [ ] Standard `data/domain/presentation` structure
- [ ] Shared components reused from `lib/shared/`
- [ ] Queue screens follow [`ui-workspace.mdc`](./ui-workspace.mdc) layout stack
- [ ] UI feedback states per [`ui-feedback.mdc`](./ui-feedback.mdc)
- [ ] Forms/tables per [`ui-patterns.mdc`](./ui-patterns.mdc)
- [ ] No raw UUIDs, enum codes, or magic color/spacing constants in presentation UI
- [ ] Shared-data mutations follow [`instant_ui_sync.mdc`](./instant_ui_sync.mdc):
      immediate success patch, scoped backend event, correct `RealtimeEventGroups`,
      targeted reconciliation, and authenticated reconnect refresh
- [ ] Cancel/failure does not patch, invalidate, or refresh shared UI state
- [ ] New realtime behavior has delta/event-group, controller, reconnect, and backend
      event-emission coverage where applicable
- [ ] Tests for controller and critical UI

